THOUGHT: The nullable `edge` parameter is dereferenced without a null check. Callers (e.g., RegionMaker) may legitimately pass null, so the safest fix is to simply return early when `edge` is null, avoiding the dereference. This will satisfy NullAway without changing behavior for non-null edges. I’ll update the method accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '20,22c\	public static void addEdgeInsn(@Nullable Edge edge, InsnNode insn) {
		if (edge == null) {
			return;
		}
		addEdgeInsn(edge.getSource(), edge.getTarget(), insn);
	}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/attributes/nodes/EdgeInsnAttr.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error(s)?" -i new_build_output.log | tail -n 20
```

